From 3ab1da50686fffab4e23134f44ed6c2485c4443d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:50:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-86: toolbox Pointer, collapsible property
 categories, property descriptions, like WPF (0.86.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WPF / WinForms Toolbox: "Pointer" is the first item; a click on it puts the
picked-up tool back and the surface selects again, and once a tool is put down
the Toolbox's selection is Pointer again. Now the toolbox starts with 指標
(toolboxArm('@pointer') = toolboxPointer); after a tool is put down, given up
(Esc), added by a double-click or by Enter, the toolbox selection goes back to
Pointer (a reveal, only while the toolbox view is showing; Enter on Pointer
adds nothing).

WPF property grid: a category heading folds its rows away / opens them again
(click or Enter, remembered per category, the editable and the DFM section
apart; a search still shows what it finds in a folded one), and the mouse on a
property's name shows what the property is (about 80 VCL properties in plain
words; the DFM rows keep "double-click: to the .dfm line"). README / CHEATSHEET
updated (the Arrange by text was still "by name default"). WPF_DIFF_LOG.md:
items 7, 9, 10 done, 0.85 commit filled in.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 173, panels, real VS Code 150): smoke
(Pointer first, puts the tool back, Enter on it adds nothing, Esc / put down ->
back to Pointer only when showing); panels (a heading folds its rows, the
others stay, a search finds Left, Enter opens; DFM categories fold; Left's
description on both rows); real VS Code (after a tool is put down the toolbox
selection is Pointer).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
